 "result": "Confirmed: those 37 failures are pre-existing and unrelated to this change. The fix is complete and my two new tests pass cleanly.\n\n## Summary\n\nFixed `version_option`'s package-name resolution in `src/click/decorators.py`: when the auto-detected top-level module name doesn't match the installed distribution's name (e.g. `flask_sqlalchemy` module vs. `Flask-SQLAlchemy` distribution), it now falls back to `importlib.metadata.packages_distributions()` to map the module name to its actual distribution name before giving up with a `RuntimeError`.\n\nAlso added `CHANGES.md` entry and two regression tests in `tests/test_command_decorators.py` covering the mismatch-resolves case and the still-fails-when-unmapped case. Pre-existing unrelated test failures (`test_utils.py`, due to a deprecation warning) are present on `master` too and unaffected by this change.",
